# 40 One-Liner Cyber Forensics MCQ Revision Points

1. Cyber Forensics is the science of collecting and analyzing digital evidence.
2. Chain of Custody ensures evidence integrity and accountability.
3. Evidence Checkout Log records all evidence transfers.
4. RAM is volatile evidence.
5. Hard disk data is non-volatile evidence.
6. Volatile evidence should be collected first.
7. First responder secures the crime scene.
8. Documentation begins immediately after incident detection.
9. Forensic duplication creates an exact bit-by-bit copy.
10. Original evidence should never be analyzed directly.
11. Write blockers prevent modification of storage media.
12. FTK Imager is used for forensic imaging.
13. Volatility is used for memory analysis.
14. Autopsy is an open-source forensic tool.
15. EnCase is a commercial forensic tool.
16. Wireshark captures and analyzes network traffic.
17. Hashing verifies evidence integrity.
18. MD5 produces a 128-bit hash value.
19. SHA-1 produces a 160-bit hash value.
20. SHA-256 is more secure than MD5.
21. Matching hash values indicate evidence integrity.
22. Mismatched hashes indicate evidence alteration.
23. Identification is the first phase of an investigation.
24. Reporting is the final phase of an investigation.
25. Containment prevents incident spread.
26. Eradication removes the threat.
27. Recovery restores normal operations.
28. Lessons Learned improves future security.
29. Signature-based detection identifies known attacks.
30. Anomaly-based detection identifies unusual behavior.
31. IDS stands for Intrusion Detection System.
32. IPS stands for Intrusion Prevention System.
33. Event Viewer stores Windows logs.
34. Deleted files can often be recovered from unallocated space.
35. Metadata provides information about files.
36. Registry stores Windows configuration information.
37. Browser history can provide investigation evidence.
38. Network logs help identify suspicious activity.
39. Memory forensics reveals running processes and malware.
40. Maintaining chain of custody is critical for court admissibility.

